WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
and resolution time to even seconds.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.600
So whenever let's say before we were taking

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.400
uh some hours, even a couple of days to respond

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.320
to a to our user request.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.880
Now we're taking I mean minutes.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.920
I think now the bottleneck is not how fast Myra

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.120
or Mach 1 can respond, but now the bottleneck

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.680
is how fast the user can respond back.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.040
So I think we switched it gears into now, uh

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.520
yeah. I mean we're pretty much responding not

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.040
only very fast, but also with uh much better

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:36.000
quality.

